WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.000
Every particle has a twin,
called its antiparticle.

2
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:07.370
It has the same mass,
but the opposite charge.

3
00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:10.590
The electron's antiparticle
is the positron.

4
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:14.200
Let a positron meet an
electron, almost at rest.

5
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.590
They annihilate.

6
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.560
In an instant, both particles are gone.

7
00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:19.920
So what comes out?

8
00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:22.680
And why is it never just one thing?

9
00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:27.560
In this mission, you'll check what must
stay the same before and after a particle

10
00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.400
meets its antiparticle.

11
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:33.790
Then you'll work out how much
energy the vanishing pair sets free.

12
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:39.240
Your mission: predict what comes out, and
explain why it is never just one thing.
